*NOTE* What is an executable? my definition is a file we can run that starts a process.

---- Windows Executables ----
Portable Executable (PE) [.exe, .dll, .scr, .cpl] - .exe are executable dlls
                                                  - .

"Scripts"                                         - .bat .cmd .py .ps1 - file extensions have registry mappings to associate with their execution strategy. There are many others.
                                                    %USERPROFILE%\documents\name.bat - cmd.exe /c name.bat
                                                    %USERPROFILE%\documents\name.cmd - cmd.exe /c name.cmd
                                                    %USERPROFILE%\documents\name.ps1 - powershell.exe -File name.ps1
                                                    %USERPROFILE%\documents\name.py  - python.exe name.py
                                                    %USERPROFILE%\documents\name.msi - msiexec.exe /i name.msi

.appx .msix .msi                                  - These are not PE format
